        <span class="lab-tag">Lab A2: extend the agent</span>
        <h3>Add a rate-limit filter to token-efficient-workshop-java</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 23px; color: var(--fg-muted); margin-bottom: 14px;"><strong>Objective:</strong> fix the session-timeout bug and add a rate-limit servlet filter using a persistent instruction file, a reusable skill or command, and an automated hook.</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Add a <code>CLAUDE.md</code> (or equivalent instruction file) with the Java conventions: constructor injection, no field injection, tests with JUnit 5.</li>
          <li>Create a skill or command for "add a servlet filter": <code>.claude/skills/add-filter/SKILL.md</code> with a description and step-by-step instructions.</li>
          <li>Add a <code>PostToolUse</code> hook that runs <code>mvn -q spotless:apply</code> to format after every edit, plus a hook that runs <code>mvn -q test</code> to keep tests green.</li>
          <li>Ask the agent to fix the session-timeout bug and add the rate-limit filter. Let it use the skill and verify the hook fires.</li>
        </ol>
        <p class="lab-out"><strong>Expected result:</strong> a working <code>RateLimitFilter.java</code>, green tests, and a reusable config that any future session can pick up without re-explaining the conventions.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="callout">
        The instruction, skill, and hook are now part of the repo. The next developer (or next session) inherits the same guardrails for free.
